From 23f57c278e6365d9c013f0975c559014f411c7a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:23:31 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] Draw a 2D document as the window draws it when the
 canvas is on a layer
Forwarded: no, Krita's README sets a moratorium on AI-assisted contributions; carried in the edition's fork,
 https://invent.kde.org/danielcamposramos/krita

A window whose canvas can be shown on the layer below it has an alpha
channel, and every canvas in it is shown through a layer: a stereo
document through the layer of its two eyes, any other through a layer with
one buffer. Two things a 2D document showed differently from a window
without the layer are fixed:

- The brush outline was painted on the transparent widget over the layer,
  and its subtracting blend inverted nothing there, so it was drawn in its
  own colour instead of the inverse of the picture under it. The
  decorations and the outline of a layer with one buffer are now painted on
  that layer's picture, with QPainter's same paint engine, so the outline
  inverts the picture as on the window. The eye framebuffer gets a stencil
  buffer for the paint engine's path fills and clips. A stereo pair keeps
  its decorations on the widget, on the screen plane.

- The separators of the dock areas were painted in the window's colour:
  QMainWindow::event() paints them before paintEvent(), and the window's
  own background, painted in paintEvent() with the Source mode, covered
  them. The background is now painted in event(), before the separators,
  as Qt paints an opaque window's background before them.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
